{
  "_comment_topbar_2026_09_07": "Gameplay top-section rebuild. Individual artist-supplied PNGs in assets/topbar/ (byte-identical copies of Downloads/New Assets/, MD5-verified, never modified) registered under the tbn_* texture ids. Each is a standalone transparent element used undistorted (aspect-fit only, no non-uniform scaling of decorative art). The Goal panel is assembled dynamically per Goal Parts/goal part instructions..txt: fixed decorative end caps (tbn_goal_left / tbn_goal_right) + a procedural rounded-blue middle whose width grows with the objective count + the GOAL header (tbn_goal_top) centred above the whole assembly. No new digit/coin/coin-pill art was supplied so those keep their existing look.",
  "_comment": "Data-driven region map for the user-supplied UI art sheets (2026-09-06 UI asset integration). The two source PNGs in assets/ui_kit/ are byte-identical copies of the artist's sheets and are NEVER modified — AssetLibrary.ui_slice(id) returns an AtlasTexture over the sub-rect named here (filter_clip on), so only the intended element shows. `rect` is [x, y, w, h] in source pixels. `nine` (optional) is [left, top, right, bottom] NinePatchRect patch margins for the pieces meant to stretch on one axis (the slider tracks). `safe` (frames only) is the content-area inset [left, top, right, bottom] in source px, measured from the frame's purple interior — screens place their content in a MarginContainer inset by these fractions so nothing overlaps the gold border. Crop bounds were derived from the sheets' alpha channels (connected-component bounding boxes + gap analysis), not estimated, and verified on magenta-background montages. NOTE: the crossed-swords reward icon on the Daily Rewards sheet has the green tick composited over it in the source and is therefore NOT cleanly separable — it is deliberately omitted; day 3 uses dr_icon_crystal instead.",
